//! ML-DSA-65 known-answer tests (KAT) — FIPS 204 keygen determinism pin.
//!
//! FIPS 204 key generation is deterministic from the 32-byte seed, so the
//! public key bytes are a stable function of the seed. These fixtures pin
//! that function for 32 seeds of the form `[i*7 + 1; 32]` (i = 0..31):
//! if the crate (or its ml-dsa dependency) ever derives a different
//! public key from the same seed, this test goes red — the earliest
//! possible signal of an implementation or dependency break, before any
//! minted token fails verification in the field.
//!
//! The fixture was generated once from ml-dsa 0.1.2 and cross-checked
//! against a second independent FIPS 204 implementation (fips204 0.5.0)
//! during the 2026-11-03 spike: same seed, byte-identical public key.
#![cfg(feature = "mldsa")]

/// (seed hex, public key hex) pairs; every key is the 1952-byte FIPS 204
/// `pkEncode` output of its seed.
